  "id": "continuum-of-care",
  "term": "continuum of care",
  "definition": "In maternal health, the continuum of care means providing connected care across the whole period of pregnancy, childbirth, and the postpartum stage rather than as separate services. This integrated approach is intended to keep care continuous, improve use of essential maternal health services, and support better outcomes for mothers and infants.",
